{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. \n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born around 1140. His father Raymond II was the Count of Tripoli and his mother Hodierna was the daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. He was still a minor when he became the Count so his mother Hodierna acted as the regent until he came of age.\n\nRaymond III played an important role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. In 1160 he was taken prisoner by the Muslims while on a raid near the Krak des Chevaliers. He was released in 1164 after a ransom was paid. In 1167 he married Eschiva of Bures the daughter of William of Bures and the widow of Walter of Saint Omer. The marriage was arranged by King Amalric I of Jerusalem.\n\n*The War with Saladin*\nIn 1170 Raymond III became the regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem for the leper King Baldwin IV. He led the army of the Kingdom of Jerusalem in several battles against Saladin the Ayyubid Sultan of Egypt and Syria. In 1177 Raymond III was defeated by Saladin at the Battle of Montgisard. In 1178 he was defeated again at the Battle of Jacob's Ford. In 1180 he made a truce with Saladin which lasted for two years.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin and the Fall of Tripoli*\nIn 1187 Raymond III joined the army of the Kingdom of Jerusalem to fight against Saladin. The army was defeated at the Battle of Hattin and Raymond III was captured by Saladin. He was released after the Battle of Hattin and fled to Tripoli. In 1187 Saladin besieged Tripoli but Raymond III was able to defend the city. However in 1187 Raymond III died and was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004263356